[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:New Year Resolutions]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.52]Lesson 50 | 第50课
[00:02.79]New Year resolutions | 新年的决心
[00:10.99]What marked the end of the writer's New Year resolutions? | 是什么宣告了作者新年决心的终结？
[00:16.81]The New Year is a time for resolutions. | 新年是下决心的时候。
[00:19.91]Mentally, at least, most of us could compile formidable lists of 'dos' and 'don'ts'. | 至少在头脑里，我们中的大多数人都会编排出一份令人敬畏的“应做”与“不应做”的清单。
[00:27.54]The same old favourites recur year in year out with monotonous regularity. | 相同的老宠幸年复一年、以单调的规律重复出现。
[00:34.27]We resolve to get up earlier each morning, eat less, | 我们决心每天早点起床、少吃一点、
[00:38.35]find more time to play with the children, do a thousand and one jobs about the house, | 多花点时间陪孩子玩、料理成百上千件家务、
[00:44.12]be nice to people we don't like, drive carefully, and take the dog for a walk every day. | 善待我们不喜欢的人、小心开车、每天遛狗等等。
[00:51.73]Past experience has taught us that certain accomplishments are beyond attainment. | 过去的经验告诉我们，某些成就是无法企及的。
[00:57.86]If we remain inveterate smokers, it is only because we have so often experienced the frustration that results from failure. | 如果我们仍改不了抽烟的老习惯，那只是因为我们已多次体验过失败带来的沮丧。
[01:07.83]Most of us fail in our efforts at sel-improvement because our schemes are too ambitious and we never have time to carry them out. | 我们中大多数人自我完善的努力都归于失败，因为我们的计划野心太大，而且根本没有时间去实施。
[01:17.37]We also make the fundamental error of announcing our resolutions to everybody | 我们还犯一个根本性的错误：把我们的决心告诉所有人，
[01:23.01]so that we look even more foolish when we slip back into our bad old ways. | 这样，当我们退回到原来的坏习惯中时，就显得更加愚蠢。
[01:29.20]Aware of these pitfalls, this year I attempted to keep my resolutions to myself. | 深知这些陷阱，今年我企图把决心秘而不宣。
[01:36.21]I limited myself to two modest ambitions: to do physical exercises every morning and to read more of an evening. | 我只给自己限定两个适度的抱负：每天早晨做体操，每晚多读点书。
[01:46.61]An all-night party on New Year's Eve provided me with a good excuse for not carrying out either of these new resolutions on the first day of the year, | 新年前夜的一场通宵聚会为我提供了很好的借口，使我在新年第一天没有执行这两项新决心中的任何一项，
[01:57.90]but on the second, I applied myself assiduously to the task. | 但第二天，我便勤勤恳恳地投入了这项任务。
[02:03.67]The daily exercises lasted only eleven minutes and I proposed to do them early in the morning before anyone had got up. | 每天的体操只持续11分钟，我打算在任何人起床之前的清晨完成。
[02:13.40]The self-discipline required to drag myself out of bed 11 minutes earlier than usual was considerable. | 把自己从床上拖起来比平常早11分钟所需的自律是相当大的。
[02:21.74]Nevertheless, I managed to creep down into the living room for two days before anyone found me out. | 不过，我成功地连续两天悄悄溜进客厅而不被人发现。
[02:31.03]After jumping about on the carpet and twisting the human frame into uncomfortable positions, | 在地毯上蹦跳一阵、把人体扭曲成各种不舒服的姿势之后，
[02:37.82]I sat down at the breakfast table in an exhausted condition. | 我筋疲力尽地坐到了早餐桌旁。
[02:42.89]It was this that betrayed me. | 正是这一点出卖了我。
[02:45.78]The next morning the whole family trooped in to watch the performance. | 第二天早晨，全家人列队进场观看表演。
[02:50.51]That was really unsettling but I fended off the taunts and jibes of the family good-humouredly and soon everybody got used to the idea. | 这确实让人不安，但我心平气和地顶住了家人的嘲讽挖苦，大家很快便接受了这个主意。
[03:00.40]However, my enthusiasm waned. | 然而，我的热情消退了。
[03:03.85]The time I spent at exercises gradually diminished. | 我花在体操上的时间逐渐减少。
[03:07.67]Little by little the eleven minutes fell to zero. | 11分钟一点一点地减少，直至降为零。
[03:12.29]By January 10th, I was back to where I had started from. | 到1月10日，我回到了起点。
[03:17.33]I argued that if I spent less time exhausting myself at exercises in the morning, | 我辩解说，如果早晨少花时间把自己搞得筋疲力尽，
[03:23.54]I would keep my mind fresh for reading when I got home from work. | 下班回家后头脑会更清醒，读书的效果会更好。
[03:28.32]Resisting the hypnotizing effect of television, | 抵制住电视的催眠作用之后，
[03:32.16]I sat in my room for a few evenings with my eyes glued to a book. | 我在自己的房间里坐了几个晚上，眼睛紧盯着书本。
[03:37.18]One night, however, feeling cold and lonely, I went downstairs and sat in front of the television pretending to read. | 然而，一天夜里，又冷又孤单，我下了楼，坐在电视机前假装看书。
[03:47.05]That proved to be my undoing, for I soon got back to my old bad habit of dozing off in front of the screen. | 那正是我垮台的开始，因为我很快便恢复了在屏幕前打瞌睡的老毛病。
[03:57.32]I still haven't given up my resolution to do more reading. | 我仍未放弃多读些书的决心。
[04:01.22]In fact, I have just bought a book entitled How to Read a Thousand Words a Minute. | 事实上，我刚买了一本名叫《如何每分钟读一千个词》的书。
[04:08.70]Perhaps it will solve my problem, but I just haven't had time to read it! | 也许它能解决我的问题，只是我一直没有时间去读它！
